From: Xun2202 <98207886+Xun2202@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 14 Oct 2026 17:36:42 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] app: scroll recorder samples threads less often and counts
 composed cells
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The 500 ms sampler walked /proc/self/task on every sample. At idle that
was about 50 ms, and about 25 ms while scrolling, so the recorder was
roughly 7% of one core. Both threads were named so their 15-character
comm was "HarmonyFramePer", and cpu_perf added them together.

Per-thread CPU is now read every fourth sample, about every 2 s. The
other samples print cpu=skip and do not touch /proc. comm is cached and
re-read only for a new tid, and stat is parsed from a reused buffer.
The sampler thread is "HarmonyPerfSmpl", so the export splits cpu_perf
(the FrameMetrics listener) and cpu_smpl (the sampler).

Each scroll segment and the stages line now include the sum and p90 of
measures, measure_ms and composed per Choreographer tick. Each per-second
line includes the composed sum and measure_ms p90. A single intended-vsync
gap longer than 1 s is an idle_hole and is not counted as missed, on the
segment, the per-second line and the overall total.

The export format is harmony-scroll-perf 3.

与 anikku-harmony 0044 同源（HarmonyFramePerf.kt 逐字节共用），Anikku 侧待移植。
